            "grounded_block": "NEX Indonesia knowledge (grounded · cite the region/topic when useful, do not embellish):\n  · [food.rendang · West Sumatra · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    Rendang is a slow-cooked beef curry from West Sumatra (Padang cuisine). Beef is simmered for hours in coconut milk with lemongrass, galangal, turmeric, kaffir lime and chilli until the liquid reduces and the meat turns dark and rich. Best found at Padang restaurants (rumah makan Padang) — the classic ordering style is a bench of small dishes brought to your table, you pay for what you eat.\n  · [indonesia.language · Indonesia · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    The official language is Bahasa Indonesia. English is common in tourist areas (Bali, Jakarta, Yogyakarta) but limited elsewhere. Learning a handful of phrases (terima kasih = thank you, permisi = excuse me, tolong = please) is warmly received.\n  · [food.nasi_padang · West Sumatra · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    Nasi Padang is the classic Padang-style presentation from West Sumatra: rice served with 10–15 small dishes brought to your table — rendang, gulai ayam (chicken curry), sambal ijo (green chilli), telur balado (spicy egg), sayur nangka (jackfruit curry) — and you pay only for what you eat. Rumah Makan Padang (Padang restaurants) are everywhere in Indonesia. Very spicy by default; ask for 'tidak pedas' if you want mild."
          }
        },
